## Why This Is Asked
This question probes a deep, practical OS concept: coordinating readers and writers on shared memory with minimal stalls and strong consistency across NUMA/container boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- Per-page versioning in the page cache
- Lock-free CAS-based fault claiming
- TLB invalidation strategies and cost control
- Read-mostly shared data and versioned updates
- NUMA-affinity and cross-container coherence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo
typedef struct {
  unsigned long version;
  void *backing;
} page_t;

int claim_fault(page_t *p){
  unsigned long v = p->version;
  return __atomic_compare_exchange_n(&p->version, &v, v+1, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
}
```

